{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.conditional_on_BorromeanCommonScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.conditional_on_BorromeanCommonScale","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L134-L140","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `BorromeanCommonScale`).** Combining the\nconjectural common-scale identification with the proved combinatorial\nper-cell ratio (`perCellRatio_eq`), the mass-channel scale factor is\nexactly `1/8` — a rigorous conditional, not a `True := trivial` stub. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanCommonScale.scale_eq_per_cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanCommonScale.scale_eq_per_cell","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L131-L131","doc":"Conjecture: the common scale equals the per-cell ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanCommonScale.scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanCommonScale.scale","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L129-L129","doc":"The conjectural mass-channel scale factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanCommonScale.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanCommonScale.mk","kind":"ctor","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L127-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanCommonScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4S3Audit.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanCommonScale","kind":"class","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L121-L131","doc":"§3b-cond conjecture class (non-degenerate per AGENTS.md §3b-cond item 5):\nthe conjectural Borromean common-scale hypothesis identifies the\nmass-channel scale factor `scale` with the per-cell ratio\n`effectiveCellCount / 8`.  This is the HYPOTHESIS (the categorical\nscale identification), not the combinatorial conclusion (proved\nunconditionally above as `perCellRatio_eq`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s4_s3_half_symmetric_projection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s4_s3_half_symmetric_projection","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L84-L106","doc":"Main result: the half-symmetric H_4 projection, restricted to\nthe S_3-trivial subspace, extracts exactly ONE of the 8 ideal\noctahedral cells in the Borromean complement tessellation.\n\nScope (2026-05-24, post-purge): combinatorial bijection only.\nThe proof states the standard S_n branching arithmetic; it\nmakes NO claim about per-cell curvature κ. The earlier\n`Yekutieli per-cell` reading (κ = −G) was purged from\nproduction on 2026-05-24 (commit 71d674da1) as non-canonical:\nPR #985 found the natural-reading bijection gives κ = +0.5,\nnot −G, and no categorical derivation supplies −G·h².\n\nPer the absorbed-into-VolDensity framing (PR #1080), the\ncanonical mass formula is m(K) = m_e · VolDensity(K, q_0)\nwith no separate λ_scale constant. This bijection is a\nstructural input that constrains VolDensity(𝓑₃)'s categorical\nrefinement at h² order; it is NOT a per-cell additive\ncorrection. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection","label":"prop:s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.perCellRatio_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.perCellRatio_eq","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L80-L82","doc":"The per-cell ratio 1/8 (one effective cell of eight total). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.effectiveCellCount_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.effectiveCellCount_eq","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L75-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3TrivialFactor_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3TrivialFactor_eq","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L71-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymTrivialS3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymTrivialS3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L68-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymTotalDim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymTotalDim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L65-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.effectiveCellCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.effectiveCellCount","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L58-L59","doc":"Effective cell count = (5/2) × (2/5) = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3TrivialFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3TrivialFactor","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The S_3-trivial projection factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymTrivialS3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymTrivialS3","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L51-L53","doc":"Total trivial-S_3 content in the half-symmetric projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymTotalDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymTotalDim","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L47-L49","doc":"Total half-symmetric dimension (weighted sum of dims). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymRepresentatives","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.halfSymRepresentatives","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L39-L45","doc":"Half-symmetric content: one of each conjugate pair + 1/2\nself-conjugate.  We track the representatives and their\ncontribution weights as rationals. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s4Irreps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s4Irreps","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L30-L37","doc":"S_4 irrep data (standard; [james1984representation] §2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprS4Irrep.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprS4Irrep.repr","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S4S3HalfSymmetricProjection.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprS4Irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprS4Irrep","kind":"instance","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a5